===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|chemistry|sciences}} Any specific [[chemical element]] or [[chemical compound]] or [[alloy]].
#: {{ux|en|Hydrogen and sulphur are both '''chemicals'''.}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial}} An [[artificial]] chemical compound.
#: {{ux|en|I color my hair with [[henna]], not '''chemicals'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=FDA moves to eliminate carcinogenic Red 3 from foods|magazine=w:Center for Science in the Public Interest|url=https://www.cspinet.org/press-release/fda-moves-eliminate-carcinogenic-red-3-foods|date=2025-01-15|passage=CSPI says the Trump Administration could take steps to protect consumers from each of these '''chemicals''' and support FDA’s broader post-market assessment efforts. It could ensure that FDA sets health-protective limits on heavy metals, like lead, arsenic, and cadmium, in foods consumed by children.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} An addictive [[drug]].

====Usage notes====
* The noun is frequently used in a slang and more specific non-technical way (2nd and 3rd definition) by the general public. Chemists and those who understand chemistry may gravitate toward the first, but the term "substance" is preferred usage.

